Private client sources from artifact_storage: NOTHING is vendored into this public repo.

crates/gsvc-mount, crates/gsvc-codec, and crates/gsvc-fs-client are resolution-only placeholders
(compile_error! bodies). The real sources live in the private tensorlakeai/artifact_storage repo and
are swapped in EPHEMERALLY only for builds that enable the features needing them (`mount`,
`git-clone`):

  * locally:  just build-cli-full   — copies the private client sources from a sibling
              ../artifact_storage checkout for the build, restoring the placeholders afterward
  * CI:       .github/actions/vendor-private-crates — mints a short-lived GitHub App token
              (ARTIFACT_STORAGE_APP_ID / _PRIVATE_KEY), sparse-checks-out the required sources,
              and swaps them over the placeholders for the job only

The swapped source compiles against the PLACEHOLDER manifests, so each placeholder Cargo.toml's
dependency list must mirror the corresponding artifact_storage crate. If upstream dependencies
change, update the placeholder manifest in the same companion change. Native filesystem SDK and
wire behavior compile entirely inside `gsvc-fs-client`; the published `tensorlake` SDK has no native
filesystem module.

Wire-format coupling still applies even without vendoring: the fast-clone client
(crates/cli/src/commands/git/fastclone.rs) and the ingest client
(crates/cloud-sdk/src/artifact_storage/ingest.rs) duplicate artifact_storage wire types
(FastCloneManifest and friends, ingest request/response shapes). If those change upstream, open
a companion PR here.

Function Agent: NO core or function-specific native-binding implementation source is vendored into
this public repo.

`crates/function-agent-core` is a resolution placeholder for the canonical private crate at
`compute-engine-internal/function-service/agent-core`. The function-agent modules included by the
combined Python and Node extensions are placeholders for CEI's canonical binding modules. The full
CEI commit in `crates/function-agent-core/CEI_REVISION` is injected ephemerally:

  * locally:  `just with-function-agent-core <command>` copies from a sibling CEI checkout and
              restores the placeholder after the command
  * CI:       `.github/actions/vendor-function-agent-core` mints a short-lived GitHub App token,
              sparse-checks out the pinned CEI crate, and stages it for the job
  * CEI CI:   the same action receives the current local CEI crate, so service and SDK acceptance
              always compile one source tree instead of coordinating source-copy branches

The placeholder manifest is checked against CEI during staging and intentionally differs only by
selecting `tls-ring` instead of CEI's `tls-aws-lc` default. Staging carries every core crate input
and both language bindings, and records an explicit SHA marker so stale files are never accepted as
trusted source. Function Service remains the durable state and fencing authority; the injected
core is its disposable worker half.
